// Title: Fake-download campaign - Inno offer-execution callback
// Rule name: T1071.001 - Inno offer-execution callback
// Classification: Hunting query
// Maturity: hunting
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceNetworkEvents
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1071.001 - Application Layer Protocol: Web Protocols
// Purpose: Identify the paired URL markers Microsoft observed in rotating Inno offer callbacks.
// Logic: Preserve Microsoft's two source-published RemoteUrl filters; the portal time picker controls the interval.
// Match proves: Defender XDR recorded a network event whose RemoteUrl matched d=inno and one offer-result marker.
// Match does not prove: fake-installer execution, successful payload transfer, offer installation, persistence,
// proxy or compute monetization, compromise, victim intent, or threat-actor attribution.
// False positives: authorized bundlers or affiliate postbacks, security testing, and RemoteUrl field-quality artifacts.
// Limits: query-string capture and target-environment prevalence are unvalidated; callbacks are individual offer results
// and may occur after child payload execution. The query does not parse or correlate session parameters.
// Validation: run the controlled paired-marker positive and single-marker negative tests in validation.md before promotion.
// Evidence claims: C003, C004, C006, C007, C008, C009, C010, C013

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl has "d=inno"
| where RemoteUrl has_any ("r=offer_execution", "r=offer_execution_fail")
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    ActionType,
    RemoteUrl,
    RemoteIP,
    RemotePort,
    Protocol,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
